bds 5,2 "Position report fine"
date 2026-10-14
preamble
    High precision three-dimensional position report, used in conjunction
    with BDS 5,1. Carries the fine position offset, the source of the data
    and the altitude.
    Source: EUROCONTROL, Mode-S Specific Services and Data Link Test Bench,
    "BDS 5,2 Position Report Fine" (Mode S Specific Service Format).

    Coding: LAT_FINE and LON_FINE are two's complement. ALT uses the same
    sign+magnitude two's complement coding as BDS 5,1.

items

    STATUS "Status"
        definition
            Validity of the report.
        element 1
            table
                0: Invalid
                1: Valid
        remark
            Single status bit covering latitude, longitude and altitude.
            Set to 0 if any of the three parameters are invalid. Identical
            to the status bit in BDS 5,1.

    FOM "Figure of Merit and Source"
        definition
            Navigational performance and source of the reported data.
        element 4
            table
                0: Loss of navigational capability
                1: RNP 20, pressure altitude
                2: RNP 5, pressure altitude
                3: RNP 1, pressure altitude
                4: Differential GNSS (10 m), pressure altitude
                5: Differential GNSS (2.5 m), pressure altitude
                6: Unassigned
                7: Unassigned
                8: Unassigned
                9: Unassigned
                10: Unassigned
                11: RNP 1, GNSS height
                12: Differential GNSS (10 m), height
                13: Differential GNSS (2.5 m), height
                14: Unassigned
                15: Unassigned
        remark
            RNP is required navigational performance as defined by ICAO.
            Suitable RNP categories have not been defined for values
            below 1, therefore CPE (circular position error) is used.
            Values 6-10 and 14-15 are unassigned.

    LAT_FINE "Latitude Fine"
        definition
            Fine latitude offset, added to the BDS 5,1 latitude.
        element 18
            signed quantity 90/16777216 "°"
        remark
            Two's complement coding, must be interpreted together with the
            corresponding parameter in BDS 5,1.

    LON_FINE "Longitude Fine"
        definition
            Fine longitude offset, added to the BDS 5,1 longitude.
        element 18
            signed quantity 90/16777216 "°"
        remark
            Two's complement coding, must be interpreted together with the
            corresponding parameter in BDS 5,1.

    ALT_SIGN "Altitude Sign"
        definition
            Sign of the altitude.
        element 1
            table
                0: Positive
                1: Negative
        remark
            Combined with ALT into a single signed value.

    ALT "Altitude"
        definition
            Pressure altitude or GNSS height, see BDS 5,2 FOM.
        element 14
            unsigned quantity 8 "ft"
        remark
            Combined with ALT_SIGN into a single signed value.
            When GNSS height is contained in this field, the pressure
            altitude can be obtained from BDS 5,1.
